{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: stop the publication loop and orphan-room alarms (simplification review 55563589, findings COST-01, COST-09). After every successful publication the Room seals a checkpoint entry (room/src/core.ts:1599), which makes headSeq exceed published_through again (core.ts:1713 arms a 60 s alarm), and publicationDue (core.ts:1517-1524) treats a lag of one entry older than 60 s as due. So an idle room publishes about every 62 seconds forever: about 42,000 publications a month, each minting and revoking two tokens, running a container push and a read-back, and adding a checkpoint entry. notes/deploy-spike.md:267 observed it live. With Artifacts operations billed at $0.15 per 1,000 from 2026-10-14 this is roughly $13 to $50 per idle room per month and most of the system's cost. Required: a checkpoint-only lag never makes publication due; the checkpoint is published with the next real entry; docs/protocol.md R-LOG-8 and R-LOG-11 amended to say so; artroom verify still accepts the result. Also: a room whose repository is gone re-arms every 60 s forever and writes publication_error each time (core.ts:1543-1591; deploy-spike.md:272-274 records such rooms left behind by every spike run). Stop scheduling publication while repo-not-found persists, raise admin attention once, and add a room teardown that unbinds and stops alarms.","body":{"conditions":"A workerd test shows an idle room after one publication arms no publication alarm until a new non-checkpoint entry exists; a test shows a room with a missing repository stops alarming after the first attention item; protocol amended; root gates pass; checker review.","target_head":"a6330262b1a609843308d9a493dbd6132d428499","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}